    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19929" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιδιαῖοι</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>officers</i> at Sparta, whose
			duties were connected with the charge of the ephebi, five in number,
			acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				3.11.2
			</span></i>; but six in Inscrr.:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίδεοι</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).32
			</span></i>
			<u>B</u>, al., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίδυοι</span></b>  ib.<i><span class="en">
				41
			</span></i>: sg. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίδυιος</span></b>  ib. <i><span class="en">
				1498.13
			</span></i> (Messenia, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>). (For <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝίδυιοι</span>, i. e.
		<i>overscers.</i>)</div>
